{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/standard-potentials/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/standard-potentials.html","area":"students","kind":"topic","title":"Standard Electrode Potentials | Chemistry","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <nav class=\"mb-4\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 transition\"><span class=\"mi -arrow-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>Back to Electrochemistry &amp; Redox</a></nav>\n    \n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-lg\">\n      <!-- Header -->\n      <div class=\"border-b pb-4 mb-6\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n          <span class=\"mi -bolt text-yellow-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"bolt\">bolt</span>Standard Electrode Potentials\n        </h1>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Understanding E° values, the electrochemical series, and predicting reaction spontaneity.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-yellow-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>• Define standard electrode potential (E°)</li>\n          <li>• Read and interpret the electrochemical series</li>\n          <li>• Calculate cell potential using standard potentials</li>\n          <li>• Predict whether a redox reaction will occur spontaneously</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Section 1: What is Standard Electrode Potential? -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-yellow-100 text-yellow-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n          What is Standard Electrode Potential?\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-3\"><strong class=\"text-yellow-600\">Standard electrode potential (E°)</strong> is the voltage measured for a half-cell under standard conditions compared to the standard hydrogen electrode (SHE).</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mt-3\">\n            <p class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Standard Conditions:</p>\n            <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n              <li>• Temperature: <strong>25°C (298 K)</strong></li>\n              <li>• Concentration: <strong>1.0 mol/dm³</strong> for solutions</li>\n              <li>• Pressure: <strong>1 atm</strong> for gases</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -info-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"info\">info</span>The Standard Hydrogen Electrode (SHE)</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">The SHE is assigned an E° value of <strong>0.00 V</strong>. All other electrode potentials are measured relative to this reference. It consists of hydrogen gas at 1 atm bubbling over a platinum electrode in 1M H⁺ solution.</p>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 2: The Electrochemical Series -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-yellow-100 text-yellow-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n          The Electrochemical Series\n        </h2>\n        \n        <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">The <strong>electrochemical series</strong> is a list of half-reactions arranged in order of their standard electrode potentials. It helps us predict the direction of redox reactions.</p>\n\n        <div class=\"overflow-x-auto mb-4\">\n          <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\">\n            <thead>\n              <tr class=\"bg-red-50\">\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-left\">Half-Reaction</th>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-center\">E° (V)</th>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-left\">Trend</th>\n              </tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr class=\"bg-red-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 font-mono\">Li⁺ + e⁻ → Li</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-center\">-3.04</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-red-600\" rowspan=\"5\">↑ Strongest Reducing Agents<br>(Easily oxidized)</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-red-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 font-mono\">K⁺ + e⁻ → K</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-center\">-2.93</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 font-mono\">Ca²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Ca</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-center\">-2.87</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 font-mono\">Na⁺ + e⁻ → Na</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-center\">-2.71</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 font-mono\">Mg²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Mg</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-center\">-2.37</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 font-mono\">Zn²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Zn</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-center\">-0.76</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 font-mono\">Fe²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Fe</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-center\">-0.44</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 font-mono\">2H⁺ + 2e⁻ → H₂</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-center\">0.00</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-center\">— Reference —</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 font-mono\">Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-center\">+0.34</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 font-mono\">I₂ + 2e⁻ → 2I⁻</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-center\">+0.54</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 font-mono\">Ag⁺ + e⁻ → Ag</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-center\">+0.80</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-green-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 font-mono\">Br₂ + 2e⁻ → 2Br⁻</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-center\">+1.07</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-green-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 font-mono\">Cl₂ + 2e⁻ → 2Cl⁻</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-center\">+1.36</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-green-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 font-mono\">F₂ + 2e⁻ → 2F⁻</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-center\">+2.87</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-200 p-2 text-green-600\">↓ Strongest Oxidizing Agents<br>(Easily reduced)</td>\n              </tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-red-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-red-700 mb-2\">More Negative E° Values</h4>\n            <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n              <li>• Stronger <strong>reducing agents</strong></li>\n              <li>• Lose electrons more easily</li>\n              <li>• Metals like Li, K, Na are very reactive</li>\n              <li>• Displace metals below them in the series</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700 mb-2\">More Positive E° Values</h4>\n            <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n              <li>• Stronger <strong>oxidizing agents</strong></li>\n              <li>• Gain electrons more easily</li>\n              <li>• Halogens like F₂, Cl₂ are very reactive</li>\n              <li>• Oxidize metals above them in the series</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 3: Calculating Cell Potential -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-yellow-100 text-yellow-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n          Calculating Cell Potential\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-3\">\n            <p class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">The Formula:</p>\n            <div class=\"bg-green-100 p-3 rounded text-center font-mono text-lg\">\n              E°<sub>cell</sub> = E°<sub>cathode</sub> - E°<sub>anode</sub>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2 text-center\">Or: E°<sub>cell</sub> = E°<sub>reduction</sub> - E°<sub>oxidation</sub></p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Important Rules</h4>\n            <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n              <li>• <strong>DO NOT</strong> multiply E° values even if you balance the equation</li>\n              <li>• The species with more positive E° will be reduced (cathode)</li>\n              <li>• The species with more negative E° will be oxidized (anode)</li>\n              <li>• If E°<sub>cell</sub> &gt; 0, the reaction is spontaneous</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-yellow-50 text-left font-semibold text-yellow-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-yellow-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2 text-yellow-600\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Worked Example: Will zinc displace copper from CuSO₄?</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-yellow-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Write the half-reactions and E° values</p>\n                  <p class=\"font-mono mt-1\">Zn²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Zn &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; E° = -0.76 V</p>\n                  <p class=\"font-mono\">Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; E° = +0.34 V</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Identify oxidation and reduction</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700 mt-1\">Zn has more negative E°, so it will be oxidized (anode)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700\">Cu²⁺ has more positive E°, so it will be reduced (cathode)</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Calculate E°<sub>cell</sub></p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">E°<sub>cell</sub> = E°<sub>cathode</sub> - E°<sub>anode</sub></p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono\">E°<sub>cell</sub> = (+0.34) - (-0.76)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono\">E°<sub>cell</sub> = +1.10 V</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-green-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                  <p class=\"text-green-800 font-semibold\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>Answer: YES! E°<sub>cell</sub> = +1.10 V (positive, so spontaneous)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 text-sm mt-1\">Zinc will displace copper from copper(II) sulfate solution.</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 4: Predicting Reactions -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-yellow-100 text-yellow-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n          Predicting if Reactions Will Occur\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-purple-200 mb-4\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -crystal-ball mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>The Simple Rule</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-3\">A spontaneous redox reaction will occur when:</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg text-center\">\n            <p class=\"text-purple-700 font-semibold\">The species being reduced has a MORE POSITIVE E°</p>\n            <p class=\"text-purple-700 font-semibold\">than the species being oxidized</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -check mr-2\" data-mi=\"check\">check</span>Reaction WILL Occur</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">E°<sub>cell</sub> &gt; 0 (positive)</p>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-xs mt-1\">The reducing agent is ABOVE the oxidizing agent in the electrochemical series.</p>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded mt-2 text-xs\">\n              Example: Zn + Cu²⁺ → Zn²⁺ + Cu ✓\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-red-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-red-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -times mr-2\" data-mi=\"close\">close</span>Reaction WON't Occur</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">E°<sub>cell</sub> &lt; 0 (negative)</p>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-xs mt-1\">The reducing agent is BELOW the oxidizing agent in the electrochemical series.</p>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded mt-2 text-xs\">\n              Example: Cu + Zn²⁺ → Cu²⁺ + Zn ✗\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 5: Video -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-yellow-100 text-yellow-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n          Video: Standard Electrode Potentials\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n          <div class=\"video-container\">\n            <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/eG6xQQfRqIM\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Practice Problems -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-yellow-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n          Practice Problems\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. Will silver react with copper(II) sulfate solution?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Ag⁺ + e⁻ → Ag &nbsp;&nbsp; E° = +0.80 V</p>\n                <p>Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu &nbsp;&nbsp; E° = +0.34 V</p>\n                <p class=\"mt-2\">For Ag to displace Cu: Ag → Ag⁺ + e⁻ (oxidation)</p>\n                <p>E°<sub>cell</sub> = (+0.34) - (+0.80) = <strong>-0.46 V</strong></p>\n                <p class=\"text-red-600 mt-1\">Since E°<sub>cell</sub> is negative, <strong>NO reaction</strong> will occur.</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. Calculate the E°<sub>cell</sub> for: Mg + 2Ag⁺ → Mg²⁺ + 2Ag</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Mg²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Mg &nbsp;&nbsp; E° = -2.37 V</p>\n                <p>Ag⁺ + e⁻ → Ag &nbsp;&nbsp; E° = +0.80 V</p>\n                <p class=\"mt-2\">Mg is oxidized (anode), Ag⁺ is reduced (cathode)</p>\n                <p>E°<sub>cell</sub> = (+0.80) - (-2.37) = <strong>+3.17 V</strong></p>\n                <p class=\"text-green-600 mt-1\">Very spontaneous reaction!</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. Which is the stronger oxidizing agent: Cl₂ or Br₂?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Cl₂ + 2e⁻ → 2Cl⁻ &nbsp;&nbsp; E° = +1.36 V</p>\n                <p>Br₂ + 2e⁻ → 2Br⁻ &nbsp;&nbsp; E° = +1.07 V</p>\n                <p class=\"mt-2\"><strong>Cl₂</strong> has the more positive E° value, so it is the stronger oxidizing agent.</p>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-xs mt-1\">Cl₂ will oxidize Br⁻ to Br₂, but Br₂ cannot oxidize Cl⁻.</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n      <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-yellow-50 to-amber-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-yellow-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n          <li>• E° values are measured relative to the Standard Hydrogen Electrode (0.00 V)</li>\n          <li>• More negative E° = stronger reducing agent (easily oxidized)</li>\n          <li>• More positive E° = stronger oxidizing agent (easily reduced)</li>\n          <li>• E°<sub>cell</sub> = E°<sub>cathode</sub> - E°<sub>anode</sub> (NEVER multiply E° values)</li>\n          <li>• If E°<sub>cell</sub> &gt; 0, the reaction is spontaneous</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n\n  \n\n<!-- Topic Tracking and Quiz System -->\n  \n\n\n<div data-bidemy=\"quiz\"></div>","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-rose-50 to-pink-100 p-4 md:p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif}\n    .content-card{-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(12px);backdrop-filter:blur(12px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.95);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);} \n    .accordion-content{max-height:0;overflow:hidden;transition:max-height 0.3s ease-out;}\n    .accordion-content.open{max-height:2000px;}\n    .step-card{transition:all 0.2s ease;}\n    .step-card:hover{transform:translateX(4px);}\n    .video-container{position:relative;width:100%;padding-bottom:56.25%;height:0;overflow:hidden;border-radius:8px;background:#f9fafb;}\n    .video-container iframe{position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;border:none;}"],"quiz":{"topicId":"standard-potentials","subject":"chemistry","passingScore":60,"questions":[{"question":"What is the standard electrode potential of the Standard Hydrogen Electrode (SHE)?","options":["-1.00 V","0.00 V","+1.00 V","+2.00 V"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The SHE is assigned E° = 0.00 V as the reference point for all other electrode potentials."},{"question":"Which element is the strongest reducing agent based on E° values?","options":["Cu (E° = +0.34 V)","Zn (E° = -0.76 V)","Li (E° = -3.04 V)","Ag (E° = +0.80 V)"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Li has the most negative E° value, making it the strongest reducing agent (most easily oxidized)."},{"question":"Calculate E°cell for: Zn + Cu²⁺ → Zn²⁺ + Cu (E°Zn = -0.76 V, E°Cu = +0.34 V)","options":["-1.10 V","-0.42 V","+0.42 V","+1.10 V"],"correct":3,"explanation":"E°cell = E°cathode - E°anode = (+0.34) - (-0.76) = +1.10 V"},{"question":"If E°cell is positive, the reaction is:","options":["Non-spontaneous","Spontaneous","At equilibrium","Impossible"],"correct":1,"explanation":"A positive E°cell indicates a spontaneous reaction that can occur without external energy."},{"question":"Which is the stronger oxidizing agent: Cl₂ (E° = +1.36 V) or Br₂ (E° = +1.07 V)?","options":["Br₂ is stronger","Cl₂ is stronger","They are equal","Cannot be determined"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Cl₂ has a more positive E° value, making it the stronger oxidizing agent (more easily reduced)."},{"question":"Will copper displace zinc from ZnSO₄ solution? (E°Cu = +0.34 V, E°Zn = -0.76 V)","options":["Yes, because Cu is less reactive","No, because E°cell would be negative","Yes, because Cu has a positive E°","It depends on concentration"],"correct":1,"explanation":"E°cell = (-0.76) - (+0.34) = -1.10 V (negative), so no reaction occurs."},{"question":"When balancing equations, should you multiply E° values?","options":["Yes, always multiply by the coefficient","Yes, but only for the anode","No, never multiply E° values","Only when there are 2 or more electrons"],"correct":2,"explanation":"E° values are intensive properties - they do NOT depend on the amount of substance, so never multiply them."},{"question":"What does a more negative E° value indicate?","options":["Stronger oxidizing agent","Stronger reducing agent","More likely to be reduced","Less reactive metal"],"correct":1,"explanation":"More negative E° means the species is more easily oxidized, making it a stronger reducing agent."}]},"tracker":{"topicId":"standard-potentials","topicTitle":"Standard Electrode Potentials","subject":"chemistry","sections":["section-1","section-2","section-3","section-4","section-5","section-6"],"quizRequired":true},"links":[]}